   "html_text": "Regarding the logical implications of Scotus’s theory, Beck 1998 argues that Scotus’s theory of the neutral proposition does not entail that he denied the principle of bi-valence since propositions are only neutral prior to creation and there is never a time in the actual world when a proposition lacks a truth-value. It is clear that Scotus does not think that the definite truth-values of propositions about future events entails determinism, since he believes that many future events are due to f",
